<!-- HERO -->
<section class="lib-hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
  <div class="lib-wrap">
    <h1 class="lib-hero-product" id="hero-title">mcp-librarian</h1>
    <div class="lib-hero-badge">v{{ versions.librarian.version }}</div>
    <p class="lib-hero-tagline">A local Markdown skill library for MCP clients</p>
    <p class="lib-hero-desc">An experimental MCP server that keeps skills on disk and builds an in-memory BM25 index. Search results identify matching sections; <code>load_section</code> returns one section, while <code>find_and_load</code> and <code>load_skill</code> return the full file. If a signing key is present, supported writes re-sign the library. Integrity status is calculated during startup or rebuild, but current load responses do not enforce it.</p>
    <p class="lib-hero-desc">Version {{ versions.librarian.version }} has no external runtime npm dependencies and is Apache-2.0. Web research and community-pack operations make network requests; automatic research from <code>find_and_load</code> is off by default.</p>
    <div class="lib-hero-actions">
      <a href="https://github.com/penumbraforge/mcp-librarian" class="lib-btn lib-btn-outline" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">View on GitHub</a>
      <a href="/librarian/wiki/" class="lib-btn lib-btn-subtle">Wiki</a>
      <a href="#install" class="lib-btn lib-btn-subtle">Quick Start &#8595;</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- QUICK START -->
<section class="lib-section" id="install" aria-labelledby="install-title">
  <div class="lib-wrap">
    <div class="section-label">Quick Start</div>
    <h2 id="install-title">Install in three commands</h2>
    <pre class="lib-pre"><code><span class="code-prompt">$</span> <span class="code-cmd">git clone</span> <span class="code-arg">https://github.com/penumbraforge/mcp-librarian.git</span>
<span class="code-prompt">$</span> <span class="code-cmd">cd</span> <span class="code-arg">mcp-librarian</span>
<span class="code-prompt">$</span> <span class="code-cmd">node</span> <span class="code-arg">bin/install.js</span></code></pre>
    <p class="lib-install-note">The installer creates <code>~/.mcp-librarian</code>, generates <code>keys/private.pem</code> and <code>keys/public.pem</code>, copies the bundled <code>getting-started.md</code> skill, and offers to configure detected Claude Code, Cursor, or Windsurf installations. The starter skill remains <code>UNSIGNED</code> until you run the signing command or a supported write triggers re-signing.</p>
  </div>
</section>

