<!-- FEATURES -->
<section class="lib-section" aria-labelledby="features-title">
  <div class="lib-wrap">
    <div class="section-label">Features</div>
    <h2 id="features-title">What it does</h2>
    <div class="lib-features-grid" role="list">

      <div class="lib-feature-card" role="listitem">
        <h3>Session-Start Catalog</h3>
        <p>After MCP initialization, the server emits a logging notification containing the installed-skill catalog. Whether a client surfaces that message, and whether its model acts on it, depends on the client.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="lib-feature-card" role="listitem">
        <h3>Web Research</h3>
        <p><code>research_topic</code> searches DuckDuckGo and fetches up to five coarsely ranked results. <code>find_and_load</code> can call that path on a weak match only when <code>autoResearch</code> is enabled. Research is returned as untrusted reference text and is never saved automatically.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="lib-feature-card" role="listitem">
        <h3>BM25 plus a heuristic score</h3>
        <p><code>find_skill</code> blends normalized BM25 relevance with a heuristic score based on token shapes, code examples, imperative steps, and optional source domains. Results point at indexed chunks; the score is not a correctness or safety rating.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="lib-feature-card" role="listitem">
        <h3>{{ versions.librarian.packs }} indexed packs</h3>
        <p>The current public index lists {{ versions.librarian.packs }} packs with {{ versions.librarian.packSkills }} skills total: one Markdown file in each pack. The registry CI checks manifest structure, basic frontmatter, headings, and bundled content-guard patterns.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="lib-feature-card" role="listitem">
        <h3>Recorded signature status</h3>
        <p>With <code>keys/private.pem</code> present, <code>create_skill</code> and a changing <code>install_pack</code> re-sign every flat skill. The store records status while loading or rebuilding. <code>skill_status</code> returns that snapshot; it does not hash the file again on each call.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="lib-feature-card" role="listitem">
        <h3>Different Network Boundaries</h3>
        <p>Web research, <code>fetch_page</code>, and <code>browse_packs</code> use the guarded fetcher. <code>install_pack</code> uses a separate downloader: direct URLs are restricted to HTTPS on <code>raw.githubusercontent.com</code> unless the operator enables arbitrary hosts. <code>GITHUB_TOKEN</code> is attached only for GitHub hosts.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="lib-feature-card" role="listitem">
        <h3>Pack Install Accounting</h3>
        <p>All remote files are fetched before writes begin, but content-guard failures reject individual skills while accepted files can still install. Same-content files are skipped and same-name files are updated, which can overwrite a local skill. The result reports installed, updated, skipped, and rejected files.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="lib-feature-card" role="listitem">
        <h3>No external runtime packages</h3>
        <p>The published package declares no external runtime dependencies and requires Node.js 22 or newer. It uses Node built-ins for stdio MCP transport, search storage, cryptography, filesystem access, DNS, and HTTP(S).</p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- TOOLS REFERENCE -->
<section class="lib-section" aria-labelledby="tools-title">
  <div class="lib-wrap">
    <div class="section-label">Tools Reference</div>
    <h2 id="tools-title">14 MCP tools</h2>
    <div class="lib-table-wrap" role="region" aria-label="MCP tools reference table">
      <table class="lib-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Tool</th>
            <th scope="col">Description</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>find_and_load</td>
            <td>Search and, above a raw-BM25 threshold, return the top skill's <strong>full file</strong>. A weak match stays local by default; opt-in auto-research returns untrusted sources but does not create a skill.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>find_skill</td>
            <td>BM25 full-text search across skill names, descriptions, categories, and content. Returns ranked results with scores.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>load_skill</td>
            <td>Load a complete skill by name. Returns content and available section slugs for <code>load_section</code>.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>load_section</td>
            <td>Load a specific section within a skill by slug path for focused, minimal context loading.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>list_skills</td>
            <td>List all installed skills with metadata, categories, integrity status, and section slugs.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>browse_packs</td>
            <td>Browse indexed skill packs with descriptions and install commands. Searchable by keyword.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>install_pack</td>
            <td>Fetch a named pack or separate <code>url</code>, screen each file with the content guard, skip exact duplicates, update same-name skills, then rebuild. Partial acceptance is possible.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>research_topic</td>
            <td>Search DuckDuckGo, assign a coarse domain tier, fetch up to five results, and return extracted text in untrusted-data markers.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>fetch_page</td>
            <td>Fetch one public HTTP(S) URL and apply a simple HTML-to-text converter. It is regex-based extraction, not a full readability parser.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>create_skill</td>
            <td>Validate, save, and index a new skill. Updates the catalog so the skill is searchable in the same session.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>validate_skill</td>
            <td>Check a skill's structure, frontmatter, and content guard compliance without saving.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>export_pack</td>
            <td>Write selected skills to disk as a shareable pack with <code>pack.json</code> manifest.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>skill_status</td>
            <td>Return the integrity snapshot recorded at the last store load or rebuild: <code>VERIFIED</code>, <code>TAMPERED</code>, or <code>UNSIGNED</code>.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>server_status</td>
            <td>Return a numeric uptime, skill count, chunk/term counts, and a limited config summary. A known bug currently reports version <code>3.0.0</code> although the package is {{ versions.librarian.version }}.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- SKILL FORMAT -->
<section class="lib-section" aria-labelledby="format-title">
  <div class="lib-wrap">
    <div class="section-label">Skill Format</div>
    <h2 id="format-title">Markdown with YAML frontmatter</h2>
    <p>Skills are flat <code>.md</code> files. The runtime uses a small frontmatter parser rather than a general YAML implementation; it recognizes <code>name</code>, <code>version</code>, bracket-list <code>category</code>, <code>description</code>, and optional bracket-list <code>sources</code>.</p>
    <pre class="lib-pre"><code><span class="code-meta">---</span>
<span class="code-key">name</span>: <span class="code-str">my-skill</span>
<span class="code-key">version</span>: <span class="code-str">1.0.0</span>
<span class="code-key">category</span>: <span class="code-str">[development, patterns]</span>
<span class="code-key">description</span>: <span class="code-str">Brief description for search results</span>
<span class="code-key">sources</span>: <span class="code-str">[https://example.com/docs]</span>
<span class="code-meta">---</span>

<span class="code-cmd">## Section Heading</span>
<span class="code-comment">Content indexed at section level.</span>

<span class="code-cmd">### Sub-Section</span>
<span class="code-comment">Finer-grained content loaded independently via load_section.</span></code></pre>
    <p class="lib-install-note" style="margin-top: 16px;"><code>##</code> and <code>###</code> headings define section slugs. <code>find_skill</code> returns matching chunks and <code>load_section</code> returns one chunk. <code>find_and_load</code> deliberately returns the full selected skill.</p>
  </div>
</section>

