    <div class="section-label">Usage Examples</div>
    <h2 id="examples-title">Illustrative client flows</h2>
    <p>These sequences are examples, not guaranteed automation. Whether tools are selected, chained, or used proactively depends on the MCP client, model, and prompt.</p>
    <div class="lib-examples-list">

      <div class="lib-example-block">
        <div class="lib-example-header">A client loads a skill</div>
        <div class="lib-example-prompt">Build me a REST API for user management</div>
        <div class="lib-example-response">
          A client exposes the catalog notification &#8594; its model calls <code>find_skill</code> &#8594; receives ranked section matches &#8594; calls <code>load_section</code> with a returned slug. Tool selection is client/model behavior, not a server guarantee.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="lib-example-block">
        <div class="lib-example-header">No local match, with auto-research enabled</div>
        <div class="lib-example-prompt">Help me set up GraphQL federation</div>
        <div class="lib-example-response">
          <code>find_and_load</code> finds no strong raw-BM25 match &#8594; the server searches and fetches up to five results &#8594; returns marked untrusted text &#8594; the client may review it or make a separate <code>create_skill</code> call. With auto-research disabled, the first call only suggests <code>research_topic</code>.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="lib-example-block">
        <div class="lib-example-header">Browse and install packs</div>
        <div class="lib-example-prompt">What skill packs are available?</div>
        <div class="lib-example-response">
          Calling <code>browse_packs</code> &#8594; 9 packs found: security-hardening, api-design, git-patterns, testing-patterns, typescript-advanced, docker-and-compose, postgres-patterns, writing-skills, prompt-engineering. A client can request installation by name.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="lib-example-block">
        <div class="lib-example-header">Custom tribal knowledge</div>
        <div class="lib-example-prompt">Create a skill about our company's deployment process</div>
        <div class="lib-example-response">
          Supply Markdown directly to <code>validate_skill</code> &#8594; review any structural or content-guard issues &#8594; call <code>create_skill</code> with a flat <code>.md</code> filename. <code>fetch_page</code> is for public URLs; its SSRF guard rejects private and loopback addresses.
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

